1q04|n|The act of recovering, regaining, or retaking possession. ; Restoration from sickness, weakness, faintness, or the like; restoration from a condition of mistortune, of fright, etc. ; The obtaining in a suit at law of a right to something by a verdict and judgment of court. ; The getting, or gaining, of something not previously had. ; In rowing, the act of regaining the proper position for making a new stroke.	v:17u7,102,16~17u7,102,16	n:gdb,44,1~gdb,44,1	N:28qu,98,4;sd7,47,4~sd7,47,4;28qu,98,4
