1qic|n|One who, or that which, regulates. ; A contrivance for regulating and controlling motion, as: (a) The lever or index in a watch, which controls the effective length of the hairspring, and thus regulates the vibrations of the balance. (b) The governor of a steam engine. (c) A valve for controlling the admission of steam to the steam chest, in a locomotive. ; A clock, or other timepiece, used as a standard of correct time. See Astronomical clock (a), under Clock. ; A member of a volunteer committee which, in default of the lawful authority, undertakes to preserve order and prevent crimes; also, sometimes, one of a band organized for the comission of violent crimes.	a:1f47,109,4;13fb,59,3;28d5,20,1~1f47,109,4;13fb,59,3;28d5,20,1	n:29lz,89,45;1f47,89,1;28d5,40,4;1m06,37,3~29lz,89,45;28d5,40,4;1m06,37,3;1f47,89,1
