1qrs|v|To have ( a notion or idea) come into the mind again, as previously perceived, known, or felt; to have a renewed apprehension of; to bring to mind again; to think of again; to recollect; as, I remember the fact; he remembers the events of his childhood; I cannot remember dates. ; To be capable of recalling when required; to keep in mind; to be continually aware or thoughtful of; to preserve fresh in the memory; to attend to; to think of with gratitude, affection, respect, or any other emotion. ; To put in mind; to remind; -- also used reflexively and impersonally. ; To mention. ; To recall to the mind of another, as in the friendly messages, remember me to him, he wishes to be remembered to you, etc. ; To execise or have the power of memory; as, some remember better than others.	s:aox,4,2~aox,4,2	d:28fg,84,11;2hq,20,9;2eq,15,32;1zkw,9,8;qd7,5,10~2eq,15,32;28fg,84,11;qd7,5,10;2hq,20,9;1zkw,9,8	D:g7l,51,20;qha,22,6;1f48,8,3;2ago,4,15~g7l,51,20;2ago,4,15;qha,22,6;1f48,8,3
